3. Functional Requirements
3.1 Data Ingestion
•	FR-1 (File Upload): The system shall allow the user to upload movies.csv.zip via Google Colab's file upload widget.
•	FR-2 (Archive Extraction & Loading): The system shall extract movies.csv from the ZIP archive using zipfile.ZipFile and load it into a pandas DataFrame (df) via pd.read_csv().
3.2 Data Exploration & Profiling
•	FR-3 (Structural Inspection): The system shall inspect dataset dimensions (df.shape — 4,803 rows, 24 columns), column names (df.columns), and data types/non-null counts (df.info(), df.dtypes).
•	FR-4 (Data Preview & Slicing): The system shall preview records using df.head(), df.tail(), df.sample(5, random_state=42), and label-based row selection (df.loc[2:7]).
•	FR-5 (Statistical Profiling): The system shall compute summary statistics for numerical and categorical columns via df.describe() and df.describe(include='all'), genre frequency counts via value_counts(), and unique budget values via unique().
3.3 Data Cleaning & Preprocessing
•	FR-6 (Missing Value Detection): The system shall calculate missing value counts per column using df.isnull().sum() and df.isna().sum().
•	FR-7 (Imputation): The system shall compute central tendency statistics (mean, median, mode) and apply mode imputation using fillna().
•	FR-8 (Duplicate Verification): The system shall check for exact duplicate rows using df.duplicated().sum() and enforce uniqueness via df.drop_duplicates(keep='first').
•	FR-9 (Column Reduction): The system shall drop unnecessary/low-variance columns — permanently removing status with inplace=True (alongside index removal, reducing columns from 24 to 22) and verifying temporary exclusion of revenue.
•	FR-10 (Data Type Optimization): The system shall convert the production_countries column from object to category data type using astype('category') to reduce memory usage.
3.4 Data Export
•	FR-11 (Export Cleaned Dataset): The system shall export the cleaned DataFrame to a CSV file named new_movies_clean.csv using df.to_csv().
4. Non-Functional Requirements
•	Performance & Memory Efficiency: Converting repetitive string columns (production_countries) to the category dtype optimizes memory consumption (baseline DataFrame memory footprint: ~900.7 KB).
•	Reproducibility: Random data sampling specifies a fixed seed (random_state=42) to ensure consistent outputs across executions.
•	Modularity & Usability: Notebook cells are structured sequentially (Upload -> Load -> Explore -> Clean -> Export) for transparent verification and viva demonstration.
